/-!
# One-Sided Ideals and the D-Class Structure of Completely 0-Simple Semigroups

This file develops the theory of the one-sided ideals defined in
`Semigroup.ZeroSimple.Ideals.Defs` — principal one-sided ideals and 0-minimal
left/right ideals — and uses them to show that all nonzero elements of a completely
0-simple semigroup are D-related (the `D = J` half of the Rees theorem).

## Main results

* `isLeast_principalLeftIdealSet`, `isLeast_principalRightIdealSet`: the principal
  one-sided ideals of `a` are the least left/right ideals containing `a`.
* `isGreenL_iff_principalLeftIdealSet_eq`, `isGreenR_iff_principalRightIdealSet_eq`:
  `a` and `b` are L- (resp. R-) related iff they generate the same principal one-sided
  ideal — the bridge to the ideal-theoretic definition of Green's relations.
* `mem_principalLeftIdealSet_iff`, `mem_principalRightIdealSet_iff`,
  `mem_principalIdealSet_iff`: adequacy of the divisibility encoding — membership
  in a principal (left/right/two-sided) ideal agrees with the corresponding
  factorization over `S¹ = WithOne S`.
* `IsZeroMinimalRightIdeal.image_mul_left`, `IsZeroMinimalLeftIdeal.image_mul_right`:
  translates of 0-minimal one-sided ideals are `{0}` or again 0-minimal.
* `IsPrimitiveIdempotent.isZeroMinimalRightIdeal`,
  `IsPrimitiveIdempotent.isZeroMinimalLeftIdeal`: at a primitive idempotent `e` of a
  0-simple semigroup, the principal one-sided ideals `eS` and `Se` are 0-minimal.
* `IsCompletelyZeroSimple.isGreenD_of_ne_zero`: all nonzero elements of a completely
  0-simple semigroup are D-related.

## References

* [J. M. Howie, *Fundamentals of Semigroup Theory*][howie1995]

The proofs formalized in this module closely follow the structure and logic
from lecture notes:

* J. D. Mitchell, *MT5863 Semigroup Theory* (lecture notes,
  University of St Andrews, 2026).
-/


